From: Test Developer <test@example.com>
Date: Thu, 31 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: tcp: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference in tcp_connect

This patch fixes a potential NULL pointer dereference that could occur
when tcp_connect is called with invalid socket state. The issue was
identified during code review and could lead to kernel panic in rare
circumstances.

The fix adds a proper NULL check before accessing the socket structure,
ensuring safe operation even in edge cases.

Signed-off-by: Test Author <test@example.com>
---
 net/ipv4/tcp_output.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/tcp_output.c b/net/ipv4/tcp_output.c
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_output.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_output.c
@@ -3500,6 +3500,9 @@ int tcp_connect(struct sock *sk)
 	struct tcp_sock *tp = tcp_sk(sk);
 	struct sk_buff *buff;
 
+	if (!sk)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	tcp_call_bpf(sk, BPF_SOCK_OPS_TCP_CONNECT_CB, 0, NULL);
 
 	if (inet_csk_connect_poll(sk))
